    {
      "id": "2",
      "type": "llm",
      "param": {
        "system": "You are a senior Python engineer and code reviewer.\nYour tasks:\n1. Treat the user input as a Python code case (it may contain extra text, explanations, or minor syntax issues).\n2. First, carefully analyze and, if needed, correct the code so that it becomes valid, idiomatic Python that can be executed.\n3. Then, mentally execute the code (do NOT mention that you are simulating). Assume a standard Python 3 environment with only standard library available.\n4. Determine what the code does when run: printed output, returned values (if a main entry point is clear), and any errors or exceptions.\n5. Output a STRICT JSON object with two fields:\n   - \"python_code\": a string containing ONLY the final, cleaned, executable Python code.\n   - \"result\": a string describing the execution result. If the code prints output, include that. If it raises an error, describe the error. If it defines functions/classes only, describe that nothing is executed by default.\n\nIMPORTANT FORMAT RULES:\n- Your entire response MUST be valid JSON.\n- Do NOT wrap it in backticks.\n- Do NOT add any extra text before or after the JSON.\n- Use double quotes for all keys and string values.\n- Escape any internal newlines in \"python_code\" as \\n.\n- Escape any internal double quotes inside strings.\n- Example format:\n  {\"python_code\": \"print(1+1)\\n\", \"result\": \"Program prints: 2\"}",
        "user": "Here is the case input that should represent Python code (possibly with extra explanation):\n\n----- BEGIN CASE INPUT -----\n{{#'1'.case_input#}}\n----- END CASE INPUT -----\n\nPlease validate/correct it as Python code, then mentally execute it and respond ONLY with the JSON object as specified."
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "3",
      "type": "code",
      "param": {
        "variables": [
          ["raw_text", ["text", "2"]]
        ],
        "outputs": [
          ["python_code", "string"],
          ["result", "string"]
        ],
        "code": "import json\n\ndef main(raw_text: str):\n\tdata = json.loads(raw_text)\n\tpython_code = data.get(\"python_code\", \"\")\n\tresult = data.get(\"result\", \"\")\n\treturn {\n\t\t\"python_code\": python_code,\n\t\t\"result\": result\n\t}"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "4",
      "type": "end",
      "param": {
        "outputs": [
          ["python_code", ["python_code", "3"]],
          ["result", ["result", "3"]]
        ]
      }
    }
  ],
  "edges": [
    ["1", 0, "2"],
    ["2", 0, "3"],
    ["3", 0, "4"]
  ]
}

