1. Profit Distribution by Product Type
Technology is the top profit contributor, generating $175.08 (nearly 62% of total profit), followed by Office Supplies at $115.89 (about 41%). In contrast, Furniture shows a significant loss of $23.08, dragging down overall profitability. This reveals a strong imbalance: just two product types—Technology and Office Supplies—drive nearly all profit, while Furniture is unprofitable and warrants review.

2. Profit Trend Over Time (by Quarter)
Profit shows significant volatility over the observed quarters, with a sharp decline from Q2 2014 (¥310.8K) to Q4 2014 (¥13.3K), followed by a dramatic drop into negative territory in Q4 2015 (–¥508.2K). A strong recovery occurred in Q4 2016 (¥414.8K), marking the highest profit in the series, though this was not sustained—subsequent quarters saw a steep fall back to near-zero or slightly negative values by Q3 2017 (–¥1.0K). Overall, the trend reflects instability with no clear long-term growth pattern, punctuated by one major rebound and recurring downturns.

